lls (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 7th District is an open seat after Republican incumbent Cory Mills lost his primary to Ryan Elijah, who now faces Democrat Bale Dalton. The district leans Republican by about five points, but the incumbent's absence removes a built-in advantage, and the national environment appears favorable to Democrats this cycle.\n\nDalton has raised roughly four times as much as Elijah and carries DCCC Red-to-Blue backing, while Elijah enters with a thinner war chest and no outside spending on either side so far. Most expert raters call the race Lean or Likely Republican, though one prominent forecaster rates it a likely Democratic flip and markets still favor the Republican by about two to one. With no reliable general-election polling, the race sits close to even with a slight Republican edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4211, "margin": -1.21}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4651, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3497, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3248, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2949, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3493, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3328, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3464, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3386, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3794, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3754, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3743, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4206, "margin": -1.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3495, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3089, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2915, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3164, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3185, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.3207, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.3242, "margin": -